Derive the following Refrigerators and Heat Pumps relation from the preceding result, showing the algebra, calculus, counting, or thermodynamic identity used at each step.
\[
0=\Delta U_{\mathrm{cycle}}
=Q_{\mathrm{sys}}-W_{\mathrm{sys}}
=(Q_C-Q_H)-(-W_{\mathrm{in}}).
\tag*{[3]}
\]
Notation: \(U\) denotes internal energy of the cyclic working substance; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(Q_C\) denotes positive heat magnitude extracted from the cold reservoir per cycle; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(Q_H\) denotes positive heat magnitude delivered to the hot reservoir per cycle; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(Q_{\mathrm{sys}}\) denotes signed net heat transferred into the working substance per cycle; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(W_{\mathrm{in}}\) denotes positive work magnitude supplied to the device per cycle; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(W_{\mathrm{sys}}\) denotes signed work done by the working substance per cycle; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(\Delta U_{\mathrm{cycle}}\) denotes internal-energy change over one complete cycle; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(\dot Q_C,\dot Q_H\) denotes positive cold-side extraction and hot-side delivery rates; unit \(\mathrm{W, W}\); \(P_{\mathrm{in}}\) denotes positive input power; unit \(\mathrm{W}\).
